.TH TELNET 1
.SH NAME
telnet \- open an interactive remote terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telnet
.RI ADDRESS " [PORT]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connect to an IPv4 address or hostname, using port 23 by default. Input and output
use a Telnet NVT stream. The client negotiates echo, suppress-go-ahead,
initial window dimensions and an ANSI terminal type. An interactive terminal
is required; terminal settings are restored when the client exits.
.PP
Press Ctrl-^ to close the connection. On many keyboards this is
Ctrl-Shift-6. Ctrl-] is reserved for the VM host emergency exit.
.PP
Telnet traffic is plaintext. Use trusted peers and networks.
Subsequent window resize notifications are not implemented.
.SH SEE ALSO
telnetd(1), ifconfig(1)
